Online Sales Dashboard Description

The Online Sales Dashboard provides a comprehensive overview of sales performance across different business dimensions. It helps users understand which regions, customer segments, product categories, order classes, and cities are contributing the most to overall sales.

1. Area Wise Sales

This section shows sales distribution across four regions: Central, East, South, and West. The West region contributes the highest share of sales at approximately 30%, followed by the East region at 30%. Central contributes around 22%, while South accounts for approximately 18%.

2. Segment Wise Sales

The dashboard compares sales across three customer segments:

Consumer – approximately 552,595
Corporate – approximately 333,366
Home Office – approximately 196,850

The Consumer segment generates the highest sales, indicating that individual customers are the largest contributor to revenue.

3. Category Wise Sales

Sales are divided into three major product categories: Furniture, Office Supplies, and Technology. Furniture contributes approximately 34%, Office Supplies around 31%, and Technology approximately 35%. Technology has the largest share, although the difference between the categories is relatively small.

4. Class Wise Sales

This chart compares sales based on shipping/order class. The categories are First Class, Same Day, Second Class, and Standard Class.

Standard Class generates by far the highest sales, followed by Second Class. First Class and Same Day contribute comparatively smaller amounts. This indicates that customers predominantly choose standard shipping.

5. City Wise Sales

The City Wise Sales chart compares sales across different cities. Sales vary significantly from one city to another, with a few cities generating substantially higher sales than the majority of locations. New York City appears to be one of the strongest-performing cities, while many other cities contribute comparatively lower sales.

Overall Dashboard Insight

Overall, the dashboard indicates that Consumer customers are the biggest source of sales, Standard Class is the most commonly associated shipping class, and sales are relatively well distributed across product categories and regions. The city-level analysis shows greater variation, suggesting that certain cities have significantly stronger sales potential than others.

The dashboard can therefore be used to identify high-performing regions, customer segments, product categories, shipping preferences, and cities and support decisions related to sales strategy, marketing, inventory, and regional expansion.
